<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  WildAnimals_Stillsand.xml                 UtinniPatches — new file 2026-09-24
  ============================================================================

  Puts the campaign's Extreme Desert Star-Wars fauna/flora/pack-animals onto
  RM_Stillsand, plus JOE_Cephalope (see below). Same shape as
  WildAnimals_Pyrelands.xml / WildAnimals_FeverWood.xml.

  WHY THIS FILE HAS TO EXIST. §7 Q11a (owner, 2026-09-22): a genuinely canon
  Star Wars name is IP and must route through the Utinni campaign patch
  layer, never the franchise-free RimMandrake tier — "the top mod without
  star wars will look precisely the same as the star wars enhanced one save
  for any star wars beasts we populate it with." So RM_Stillsand may not
  carry this cast inline, and at Phase B the RUT_ExtremeDesert twin that
  currently carries it dies and RM_Stillsand takes the tiles. Without this
  patch in place by then, the Extreme Desert would lose all 13 of its fauna
  rows, all 3 of its flora rows and all 5 of its pack-animal rows on the
  live world.

  🔑 SOURCE OF TRUTH: every defName and weight below is copied from
  RUT_ExtremeDesert.xml's own wildAnimals/wildPlants/allowedPackAnimals
  (frozen 2026-09-24), the roster the world runs on today. STILLSAND_RM_MOD_BUILD_1's
  own written §3 table (dated 2026-09-23) names three of these rows under
  STALE pre-rename defNames — RSW_Spineroller, RSW_Stareling, RSW_Voltmaw — a
  same-day rename (NONCANON_BEAST_RENAME_1, f7cf979ab, 2026-09-24) landed
  between that table being written and this file, renaming them to RSW_Kudda,
  RSW_Ikee and RSW_Vozzik respectively (same commonalities, same rows). This
  file follows the live def, not the item's now-stale table.

  13 wildAnimals rows, all mandrake.rsw.swbestiary (our own RSW_ ports):
    RSW_Kudda 0.3, RSW_Kreetle 0.2, RSW_WarWyrm 0.2, RSW_KraytDragon 0.15,
    RSW_Ikee 0.15, RSW_GraniteSlug 0.1, RSW_Scurrier 0.1, RSW_Gizka 0.01,
    RSW_GreaterKraytDragon 0.001, RSW_Vozzik 0.0005, RSW_TruffleMole 0.5,
    RSW_SandLion 0.5, RSW_Drazzik 0.05

  1 wildAnimals row with no MayRequire — JOE_Cephalope 0.5. Flagged, not an
  RSW_/SW_/RUT_ name, but its ThingDef/PawnKindDef live in THIS SAME MOD
  (Defs/Absorbed_Cephaloids/Absorbed_Cephaloids_Defs.xml), not in a
  RimMandrake mod — wiring it inline on RM_Stillsand would give a
  RimMandrake-tier def an undeclared hard dependency on Utinni content
  (unresolvable on a planet with no Ash'karr loaded, failing §3a's own
  test). STILLSAND_RM_MOD_BUILD_1 flagged this as UNCERTAIN rather than
  deciding it; routing it here avoids inventing a fix (moving the def) while
  keeping RM_Stillsand safe standalone. No MayRequire guard needed — this
  patch file only ever loads alongside its own target def.

  3 wildPlants rows, all mandrake.rsw.swbestiary:
    RSW_Plant_Bloddle 0.05 (genuine SW canon — Tatooine bloddle, SWAC donor)
    RSW_LightPipeNub 0.1, RSW_Ollim 0.01 — the biome's OWN invented signature
    flora (EXTREME_DESERT_SIGNATURE_FLORA_1), not genuine Star Wars canon.
    STILLSAND_RM_MOD_BUILD_1 flags these as strong candidates to move to the
    RimMandrake tier (renamed off RSW_) per Q11a's "invented content is
    RimMandrake-tier, prefix notwithstanding" — flagged, not decided here.
    Left at their current location (RSW_, mandrake.rsw.swbestiary) and
    routed the same way as the genuine-canon row above, pending that call.

  5 allowedPackAnimals rows, all mandrake.rsw.swbestiary:
    RSW_Bantha, RSW_Ronto, RSW_Eopie, RSW_Jamel, RSW_Falumpaset
    (DESERT_PACK_ANIMALS_FOR_TRADERS_1 — without this list, no trader
    caravan ever generates here; RUT_ExtremeDesert.xml's own comment).

  ⚠️ A patch that matches nothing logs nothing (PatchOperationConditional
  returns true on no match) — validate with
  skills/rimworld-modding/scripts/validate_patch.py against the live def
  dump and the full active mod set before trusting a clean log.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional" MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">
    <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_Stillsand"]/wildAnimals</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_Stillsand"]/wildAnimals</xpath>
      <value>
        <RSW_Kudda>0.3</RSW_Kudda>
        <RSW_Kreetle>0.2</RSW_Kreetle>
        <RSW_WarWyrm>0.2</RSW_WarWyrm>
        <RSW_KraytDragon>0.15</RSW_KraytDragon>
        <RSW_Ikee>0.15</RSW_Ikee>
        <RSW_GraniteSlug>0.1</RSW_GraniteSlug>
        <RSW_Scurrier>0.1</RSW_Scurrier>
        <RSW_Gizka>0.01</RSW_Gizka>
        <RSW_GreaterKraytDragon>0.001</RSW_GreaterKraytDragon>
        <RSW_Vozzik>0.0005</RSW_Vozzik>
        <RSW_TruffleMole>0.5</RSW_TruffleMole>
        <RSW_SandLion>0.5</RSW_SandLion>
        <RSW_Drazzik>0.05</RSW_Drazzik>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <!-- JOE_Cephalope — no MayRequire, see header. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_Stillsand"]/wildAnimals</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_Stillsand"]/wildAnimals</xpath>
      <value>
        <JOE_Cephalope>0.5</JOE_Cephalope>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional" MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">
    <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_Stillsand"]/wildPlants</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_Stillsand"]/wildPlants</xpath>
      <value>
        <RSW_Plant_Bloddle>0.05</RSW_Plant_Bloddle>
        <RSW_LightPipeNub>0.1</RSW_LightPipeNub>
        <RSW_Ollim>0.01</RSW_Ollim>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional" MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">
    <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_Stillsand"]/allowedPackAnimals</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_Stillsand"]/allowedPackAnimals</xpath>
      <value>
        <li>RSW_Bantha</li>
        <li>RSW_Ronto</li>
        <li>RSW_Eopie</li>
        <li>RSW_Jamel</li>
        <li>RSW_Falumpaset</li>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
